er a Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) if not addressed promptly.\n\n### Severity Breakdown by Department\n------------------------------------\n\n| Department | Minor | Major | Critical |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cardiology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Dermatology | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n| Emergency | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| General Medicine | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Gynaecology | 4 | 1 | 0 |\n| Neurology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n\n### Recommended Actions\n------------------------\n\n1. **Dermatology**: Address the 2 critical breaches, including failure to obtain written authorization before disclosing PHI and missing informed consent for high-risk procedures.\n2. **Gynaecology**: Review and address the 4 minor breaches in compliance with HIPAA regulations.\n3. **Emergency**: Investigate and address the 1 critical breach related to missing informed consent for high-risk procedures.\n\n**Consolidated Risk Dashboard**\n=============================\n\n### Top 3 Urgent Items Across All Domains\n-----------------------------------------\n\n1. **Dermatology**: Address the 2 critical violations, including failure to obtain written authorization before disclosing PHI and missing informed consent for high-risk procedures.\n2. **Gynaecology**: Review and address the 4 minor breaches in compliance with HIPAA regulations.\n3. **Emergency**: Investigate and address the 1 critical breach related to missing informed consent for high-risk procedures.\n\nNote: The above dashboard is generated based on the provided data from the domain agents and SQL results.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the severity breakdown of compliance violations across different departments, and which department is currently exhibiting the highest volume of Critical JCI audit findings?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '**Compliance Dashboard**\n========================\n\n### Critical Violations\n------------------------\n\n* **Dermatology**: 2 Critical violations, including missing consent for high-risk procedures affecting more than 5% of applicable procedures.\n\n### Severity Breakdown by Department\n------------------------------------\n\n| Department | Minor | Major | Critical |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cardiology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Dermatology | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n| Emergency | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| General Medicine | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Gynaecology | 4 | 1 | 0 |\n| Neurology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n\n### Recommended Actions\n-------------------------\n\n1. **Dermatology**: Address the Critical JCI audit findings related to missing consent for high-risk procedures affecting more than 5% of applicable procedures.\n2. **Gynaecology**: Review and address the Minor breaches, which may be contributing to a higher overall risk profile.\n3. **Emergency**: Investigate and address the Critical breach related to PHI disclosure without valid patient authorization.\n\n**Patient Safety Dashboard**\n==========================\n\n### Department with Highest Volume of Critical JCI Audit Findings\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n* **Dermatology**: Currently exhibiting the highest volume of Critical JCI audit findings, with a total of 2 breaches.\n\n### Severity Breakdown by Department\n------------------------------------\n\n| Department | Minor | Major | Critical |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cardiology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Dermatology | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n| Emergency | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| General Medicine | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Gynaecology | 4 | 1 | 0 |\n| Neurology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n\n### Recommended Actions\n-------------------------\n\n1. **Dermatology**: Address the Critical JCI audit findings related to missing consent for high-risk procedures affecting more than 5% of applicable procedures.\n2. **Gynaecology**: Review and address the Minor breaches, which may be contributing to a higher overall risk profile.\n3. **Emergency**: Investigate and address the Critical breach related to PHI disclosure without valid patient authorization.\n\n**Consolidated Risk Dashboard**\n=============================\n\n### Top 3 Urgent Items Across All Domains\n------------------------------------------\n\n1. **Dermatology**: Address the Critical JCI audit findings related to missing consent for high-risk procedures affecting more than 5% of applicable procedures.\n2. **Gynaecology**: Review and address the Minor breaches, which may be contributing to a higher overall risk profile.\n3. **Emergency**: Investigate and address the Critical breach related to PHI disclosure without valid patient authorization.\n\nNote: The above dashboard is generated based on the provided data from the domain agents and SQL results.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the severity breakdown of compliance violations across different departments, and which department is currently exhibiting the highest volume of Critical JCI audit findings?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "**Compliance Dashboard**\n=======================\n\n### Critical Compliance Violations\n#### Dermatology has the highest volume of Critical JCI audit findings\n\n* Department: Dermatology\n* Severity: Critical\n* Violation Count: 2\n\n### Severity Breakdown by Department\n\n| Department | Minor | Major | Critical |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cardiology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Dermatology | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n| Emergency | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| General Medicine | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Gynaecology | 4 | 1 | 0 |\n| Neurology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n\n**Patient Safety Dashboard**\n==========================\n\n### Critical JCI Audit Findings\n#### Dermatology has the highest volume of Critical JCI audit findings\n\n* Department: Dermatology\n* Severity: Critical\n* Violation Count: 2\n\n### Severity Breakdown by Department (same as Compliance)\n\n| Department | Minor | Major | Critical |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cardiology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Dermatology | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n| Emergency | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| General Medicine | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Gynaecology | 4 | 1 | 0 |\n| Neurology | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n\n**Consolidated Recommended Actions**\n=====================================\n\nBased o